53:A methodological overview of our approach is shown in Supplementary Fig. S1 and full details are provided in the Supplementary Methods. Brie /uniFB02 y, for each participant, we estimated normative models to predict vertex-wise cortical thickness as a function of age and sex plus nuisance covariates including full-scale IQ, plus dummy coded site variables and the Freesurfer Euler number (a proxy for scan quality) using Gaussian process regression. Then, we estimated normative probability maps (NPMs), which quantify the deviation from normative CT, by subtracting the predicted from true CT, divided by the estimated variance at each vertex to construct a subject- and vertexspeci /uniFB01 c Z -score.
